  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a noun or with する. Almost always carries a critical or cautionary nuance — the love described is seen as excessive or unhealthy. The kanji {溺|おぼ}れる means \"to drown,\" so the word literally evokes being drowned in love.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {溺愛|できあい}する (to dote excessively on)\n- {溺愛|できあい}ぶり (the extent of one's doting)\n- {子|こ}どもを{溺愛|できあい}する (to dote on one's child)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {可愛|かわい}がる: to cherish — positive and natural affection without the negative connotation\n- {甘|あま}やかす: to spoil — focusing on permissive parenting rather than the emotional intensity",
